WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.133
-You got so much going on.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.267
-A lot, a lot, a lot.
-You got a lot going on.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.100
"Easter Sunday"
is out this Friday.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.133
-Yes.
-In theaters.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.501
-Unbelievable.
-This is a big deal.

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:11.100
Your Funny is Funny world tour,
selling out arenas.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.334
Arenas.
-I know, I know, I know.

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:13.501
It's crazy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:15.934
Even saying it.
-That's --

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.901
How is that for you,
doing arenas?

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.434
-You know, you got to bring
the energy up.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.300
It's not like a club.
You know what I mean?

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.534
I'm used to coffee houses
and just telling jokes.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:28.267
But now it's like, you got
to look up to section 300.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:30.501
They really think I'm talking
to them, but I'm not.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:31.968
-Yeah, but it's a lot of people.
-It feels good.

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:33.100
-Yeah.
-I'll even point,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.300
and they're like, "me?"
"Yeah, you!"

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.467
-Yeah, it's 18,000 people.

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:40.033
If you go to jokoy.com
for more ticket info.

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:43.501
Who was your comedy influences
when you started,

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:45.300
when you were growing up?
-I mean, of course it's gonna be

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.534
Richard Pryor on the tapes,
and then when I got HBO

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:51.400
for free, like on a weekend --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.133
That's what broke people did
back in the '80s,

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.334
for all you young kids that
don't know what that is.

00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:57.667
-Yeah.
-You remember they would give

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.868
free HBO on the weekend?
-"We get HBO this weekend?"

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:02.868
-Like, "What? Where's the tape,
let me record everything!"

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:03.868
-Everything.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.901
[ Both laugh ]
And I'll get --

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:07.467
You remember? You would break
the little square tab.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.567
-Yeah.
-Remember? It would be like --

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:09.701
-And then,
if you want to tape over,

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:11.000
you had to put Scotch tape
over the tab.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.501
-Over the ta-- yes!
-It was a big deal.

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.467
-And I recorded "Delirious,"
and I would watch that

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:15.767
probably a million times.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:18.901
I fell in love
with Aunt Bunny and Uncle Gus.

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.734
-Wow.
-And mom with the bionic ear.

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.767
All that.
I was like, "That's my family."

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.300
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.234
-And literally got to see him
perform when I was 15.

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:29.467
-Really?
-Yep, I saw him --

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.167
-Your parents took you?
-Nope.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:34.100
Okay, here's another thing
for you young kids out there.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.567
We didn't have the Internet.
Ticketmaster was actually

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:39.234
a little kiosk
inside of a department store,

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:41.868
and you had to phone
your phone call in.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.934
You had to buy it on line
with a credit card,

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.968
and then they left it up,
the person selling it,

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:47.400
to figure out
if that was really you

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.400
that owned the credit card
just by your voice.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.968
-Wow.
-So I just --

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:53.100
I was 15,
and I used my mom's voice.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.534
There was no way
they could tell.

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:55.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.501
I just --
There's no way they would --

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:59.367
I was just, [ Filipino accent ]
"I'd like two tickets to..."

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:01.567
[ Laughter ]
"...the Eddie Murphy

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:05.534
comedy show, please."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:06.834
[ Normal voice ]
I swear!

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:09.300
This is not even a lie, Jimmy.
And then they were like,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.634
"Okay. Um, well, what kind of
seats would you like?"

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:13.634
[ Filipino accent ]
"Oh, the best money can buy."

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.767
[ Laughter ]
"Please."

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.601
[ Normal voice ] And, literally,
I got tickets to see

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:20.100
"Eddie Murphy Raw"
at the Seattle Coliseum.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.601
-Wow.
-I remember my mom driving me,

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:24.234
'cause we lived in Tacoma.
And she thought it was a movie,

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:25.701
and it was me and my best friend
at the time.

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:26.968
And we were driving,
and she's like,

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:28.767
[ Filipino accent ] "This is
a long way for a movie."

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:31.234
[ Laughter ]
"One hour? You couldn't get

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.734
a theater closer to the house?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.200
[ Normal voice ]
And then dropped me off.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.400
And she was like,
"This is a concert!

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.701
Oh, my God!"
'Cause there was no cellphones,

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:41.000
so she had to drive around
for like two hours.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.601
-Yeah.
-"You better be out here

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.067
in two hours!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.400
-Mad at you.
-Swear!

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.133
That's how it went down.
-Here's the best part.

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:51.434
Here we are --
what, is it 35 years later?

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.968
-35 years later.
-And you yourself

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.467
have played that arena.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:58.067
-So, look at that.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.801
-The Climate Pledge Arena.

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:04.400
-But I was --
Eddie was sitting here --

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.767
Eddie was on stage here,
and I was sitting right there.

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:09.367
And before we --
before that show started,

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:12.467
I took my son, and we sat
in the same exact seats

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.167
where I sat and saw Eddie.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:15.834
-Isn't that cool?
Come on.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:18.434
That's the greatest.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:20.000
I'm getting teary-eyed
thinking about it right now.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.234
-Yeah, it's the best.
I mean, it's such a fun ride

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:23.267
to do all this.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:24.901
Because you remember
starting out.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.400
I mean, when did you start
doing stand-up?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.300
-I started in 1989.
-Yeah.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.400
-Yep.
-Teenager.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.100
-Oh, the worst.
I had baby hair.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.267
I had a little Asian baby hair,
and I let it grow for like

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:37.434
two weeks,
and I used this mascara.

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.434
Because it was at a bar.
The bar's still there.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.133
It's on Tropicana and Eastern.
I swear!

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:43.334
-You used mascara
on your wispy mustache?

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.067
-Yeah.
It was so wispy, too.

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:46.400
[ Laughter ]
It was so wispy.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.033
-It was flying around.
-Yeah, when the doors opened,

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:51.400
my mustache opened, too.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.200
It would open and go, "Hello,"
and then close.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.501
[ Laughter ]
It was so bad.

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:59.501
And I remember darkening it
and going to this bar.

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.934
I was like 18, 19.
And I remember

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.200
"Don't order a drink," because
they might ask for your I.D.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.834
And I went up, and I bombed.
I bombed so bad.

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:08.834
All I could talk about was,
I think, condoms?

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.434
I thought that was edgy.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:12.534
I was like 18 years old,
buying con--

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:14.567
No one laughed
at the condom joke.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.801
The guy before me was
a Lionel Richie impersonator.

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.667
He crushes it.
-Ugh!

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.067
-Yeah, I lost
to a Lionel Richie impersonator.

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:22.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:26.200
And when I was onstage, while I
was bombing, my mouth got dry,

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.133
and my tongue started sticking
to the roof of my mouth.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:30.634
And I go --
And I started talking about it.

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.767
I was like, "Hey, you ever --
your mouth get so dry,

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:34.267
it sticks to the roof
of your mouth?"

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:38.067
And this lady at the bar goes,
"Put a condom on it!"

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.467
And crushes!
-Crushes.

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:45.234
-Crushes! Crushes with the joke
I bombed with!

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:47.300
[ Laughter ]
I was, like, so --

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.467
-That's when you know it's bad.
-Humiliating!

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:51.868
Was like,
"How did it work for you?

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:53.367
I wrote it!"
-Yeah.

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:55.033
It's good delivery right there.
-Yes!

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.901
And then the Lionel Richie guy
was like, "Hey, man,

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:59.667
you were bad tonight, but you've
got good stage presence."

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:02.200
I'm like, "Thanks."
But thank God he said it

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.000
'cause if he didn't say that,
I probably would've just had

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.234
a really nice mustache.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:08.300
-Look at you now.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:09.567
Look at you now
selling out arenas.

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:10.901
Come on, buddy --
Funny is Funny.

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:12.067
Come on, bud.
-Thank you.

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:13.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:16.434
I want to talk about your movie.

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:17.868
-Yes.
-This is a big deal.

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:19.067
This is in theaters this Friday.

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.901
It's called "Easter Sunday."
-Unbelievable.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:24.400
-Tell the story, if you can,
how -- I'll set you up.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.501
But how is Steven Spielberg
involved in your life?

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:29.000
And this is --
-This is nuts.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.267
-It's great.
-So, my special came out

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:33.234
on Netflix,
called "Coming in Hot,"

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:35.901
and we get a call from Amblin.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.400
And Amblin's like,
"Hey, we want a meeting."

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.567
So, you know,
I thought it was a general.

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:39.601
-Yeah.
-I thought it was --

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:40.801
Yeah, it's Steven's company.

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:43.300
I call him Steven.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.434
Steve!
-Since when?

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:46.968
-Hey, Steve!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:48.834
-Have you ever met him?
-No. No.

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:51.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:53.067
-Come on, bud.

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:57.033
[ Laughter continues ]

00:05:57.033 --> 00:06:00.467
-Oh, that was so good!

00:06:00.467 --> 00:06:01.601
Oh, my God!

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:03.300
I have an e-mail,
and I'm gonna frame it!

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.400
It's amazing!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.000
No, but what happened was,
they brought me in for --

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:14.534
That was so good!

00:06:14.534 --> 00:06:16.868
I'm crying right now!
Okay, okay, I'm sorry.

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:18.133
I'm sorry.
All right.

00:06:18.133 --> 00:06:19.534
-All right,
so he sees your special.

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:20.701
-Why'd you have to call me out?!

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:21.901
-I don't know, I don't know,
I don't know.

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:23.367
[ Laughter ]
I didn't plan on that.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:24.968
I didn't plan that.
Sorry.

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:27.234
-So, we get the call.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:27.234 --> 00:06:28.834
Okay. All right, all right.
Stop, stop, stop.

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:31.734
Okay, so we get the call,
and I think it's a general.

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:33.534
And we go in.
And, literally,

00:06:33.534 --> 00:06:34.767
it's me and my manager,
and it's, like,

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:36.934
every other person that's
walking up to me is like,

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:38.901
"Steven can't
stop talking about you,"

00:06:38.901 --> 00:06:40.334
"Steven loves your comedy,"

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:42.000
"Steven thinks you're so funny."

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.000
Like, literally,
"Steven, Steven, Steven."

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.100
We get to the meeting.
Holly and Jeb's in the meeting,

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.000
and they're like,
"Steven loves your comedy."

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.934
And I'm like -- I stop them.

00:06:50.934 --> 00:06:53.067
And I'm like,
"Look, are we talking about

00:06:53.067 --> 00:06:54.767
Steven from accounting?"

00:06:54.767 --> 00:06:56.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:58.734
-"Or..."
-"'Cause there's no way you're

00:06:58.734 --> 00:07:02.400
talking about 'E.T.' Steven?"
-The one and only.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.033
-And they're like,
"No, it's Steven."

00:07:04.033 --> 00:07:05.467
And they're like,
"He's been telling everyone

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:07.834
to watch your special,
and he loves you,

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:09.701
and he wants
to make a movie with you.

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:11.767
And what movie idea you have?"

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:13.834
And I pitched "Easter Sunday"
in the room.

00:07:13.834 --> 00:07:15.601
They bought it in the room.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.567
And then, literally,
we went to lunch --

00:07:17.567 --> 00:07:20.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.968
It's crazy.

00:07:21.968 --> 00:07:24.834
We went to lunch,
and even then we're like,

00:07:24.834 --> 00:07:26.334
"Okay.
This isn't gonna happen."

00:07:26.334 --> 00:07:28.267
And then we go to lunch, and
then Holly calls and is like,

00:07:28.267 --> 00:07:29.601
"All right,
we're making moves right now.

00:07:29.601 --> 00:07:31.734
We're gonna look --
find a writer.

00:07:31.734 --> 00:07:33.067
We're gonna start
looking for your director."

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:34.701
And I'm like, "What?"

00:07:34.701 --> 00:07:36.300
And then the pandemic hit.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.133
Everything shut down.
I'm like, "Oh, there we go.

00:07:38.133 --> 00:07:40.067
Yeah, here goes that dream.

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:41.801
It's not gonna happen."
And they didn't care.

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:43.033
They're like,
"When something opens up,

00:07:43.033 --> 00:07:44.067
we're gonna make this movie."

00:07:44.067 --> 00:07:46.734
And Vancouver opened up,
and right away...

00:07:46.734 --> 00:07:48.467
-He made it.
-He made the movie, yeah.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:50.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Eight months later.

00:07:50.167 --> 00:07:52.267
-Eight months later.
-You've got a great director.

00:07:52.267 --> 00:07:54.300
-Jay, uh --
-Jay Chandrasekhar.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.767
-Jay Chandrasekhar is one of
the funniest dudes out there.

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:58.801
-And I was with him last night,
and he said he wanted me

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:00.133
to tell you
that he loves you so much.

00:08:00.133 --> 00:08:01.300
-I love that dude, man.
-Yeah.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:02.400
-He's one of
the funniest dudes ever, man.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.801
-He's incredible.
-What a great story.

00:08:04.801 --> 00:08:07.167
You're making some history here.

00:08:07.167 --> 00:08:09.133
Tell everyone what
"Easter Sunday" is all about.

00:08:09.133 --> 00:08:11.033
-Well, it's just --
it's a family.

00:08:11.033 --> 00:08:13.968
It's my family.
It's like, yeah, we're Filipino.

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:16.868
And it's specifically Filipino
but it's not specific.

00:08:16.868 --> 00:08:19.000
You know what I mean?
It's people that we live with.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.767
We're all in here right now,
we're hanging out.

00:08:20.767 --> 00:08:22.467
-Yeah.
-The lights are off.

00:08:22.467 --> 00:08:24.534
We're all the same color.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.534 --> 00:08:26.467
-Yeah.
-You turn the lights on,

00:08:26.467 --> 00:08:28.934
all of a sudden, we're separate,
and it doesn't makes sense.

00:08:28.934 --> 00:08:30.767
So that's
what this story is about.

00:08:30.767 --> 00:08:33.834
It's just a story about a family
that happens to be Filipino.

00:08:33.834 --> 00:08:35.767
We're gonna laugh about it,
we're gonna cry.

00:08:35.767 --> 00:08:38.901
We're gonna enjoy their pain,
and we're gonna enjoy their joy.

00:08:38.901 --> 00:08:41.667
And you're gonna realize
that a mother is a mother,

00:08:41.667 --> 00:08:45.133
a son is a son, and a family is
a family no matter what you are.

00:08:45.133 --> 00:08:46.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:46.634 --> 00:08:49.200
-That's great.
I want to show --

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.467
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:50.467 --> 00:08:52.801
Here's Jo Koy
and Tiffany Haddish

00:08:52.801 --> 00:08:55.033
in "Easter Sunday."
Take a look at this.

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:58.133
-License and registration.

00:08:58.133 --> 00:08:59.501
Joe?

00:08:59.501 --> 00:09:01.000
[ Laughing ]
Is that you, Joe?

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.467
-Vanessa!
-Yes.

00:09:02.467 --> 00:09:04.734
-Wow.
Man, you're a cop now?

00:09:04.734 --> 00:09:07.200
-Yeah, have been
for the last 10 years.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.868
You would've known that
if you wouldn't have ghosted me

00:09:08.868 --> 00:09:11.067
the way you did.
-Yeah.

00:09:11.067 --> 00:09:12.801
-And this your dad?
-Yeah.

00:09:12.801 --> 00:09:14.501
-You know me and your daddy,
we used to be

00:09:14.501 --> 00:09:16.334
real intimate back in the day.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:16.334 --> 00:09:17.334
-Oh, really?

00:09:17.334 --> 00:09:19.133
-Yeah, I could've been
your mama.

00:09:19.133 --> 00:09:21.300
But clearly I'm not.
I'm not.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.601
Yeah.
Joe Valencia.

00:09:23.601 --> 00:09:25.267
-Yes.
-I can't believe it.

00:09:25.267 --> 00:09:27.968
In a Subaru, at that.

00:09:27.968 --> 00:09:29.334
What happened?
You just gave up, huh?

00:09:29.334 --> 00:09:30.434
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.434 --> 00:09:31.834
You know,
when I saw this Subaru,

00:09:31.834 --> 00:09:34.133
I was thinking to myself,
"That gotta be two ladies

00:09:34.133 --> 00:09:35.300
and a Labradoodle."
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.167
But nope!
It's you, Joe.

00:09:37.167 --> 00:09:38.434
-Yeah, it's me.
-It's you, Joe.

00:09:38.434 --> 00:09:40.100
-It's me, Vanessa.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.801
-Get the hell out the car!

00:09:41.801 --> 00:09:43.834
-Yeah, that's exactly right!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:43.834 --> 00:09:45.467
Jo Koy, everybody!

00:09:45.467 --> 00:09:48.300
"Easter Sunday"
is in theaters this Friday.

